  "worked_solution": "First, we rewrite our Fourier series as\n\n$$\nf(x)\u223c\\frac{2}{\\pi }-\\frac{4}{\\pi }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{4{n}^{2}-1}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}\u2061(2nx).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that at $x=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(2n\\cdot 0)=\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(0)=1.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is $\\text{continuous}$ at $x=0,$ the corresponding Fourier series converges to \n\n$$\nf(0)=0.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0) & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }-\\frac{4}{\\pi }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{4{n}^{2}-1}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}\u2061(2n\\cdot 0) \\\\ 0 & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }-\\frac{4}{\\pi }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{4{n}^{2}-1}\\cdot 1 \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\pi } & =-\\frac{4}{\\pi }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{4{n}^{2}-1} \\\\ {\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{4{n}^{2}-1} & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
